         <Description>The Hinode Solar Optical Telescope Filtergraph (SOT-FG) Level 0 FGSIV FITS data product contains uncalibrated Stokes I and Stokes V images acquired with the Narrowband Filter Imager (NFI) in shutterless observing mode. The product is identified by DataCode FGSIV and OBS_TYPE='FG shutterless I and V', distinguishing it from the shuttered FGIV product. The FITS Primary HDU contains a three-dimensional image array with two image planes representing Stokes I and V. Shutterless readout provides rapid polarimetric imaging over a restricted field of view; image dimensions vary with observation settings. The inspected Level 0 FITS headers identify the shutterless observing mode with FGMODE='shutterless' and GEN_ID=32. The observing spectral line and wavelength offset are identified by the FITS keywords WAVE and WAVEOFF, respectively. The Level 0 images precede ground-based scientific calibration.</Description>
